gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.05284442474420791,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0648989246075502,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":1.2667141838916607,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.07349,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":49.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Alector, Inc., a clinical stage biotechnology company, develops therapies to counteract the progression of neurodegeneration in the United States. Its pipeline includes Nivisnebart, an investigational human recombinant monoclonal antibody for treating prevalent neurodegenerative diseases; AL137, an anti-amyloid beta antibody paired in preclinical development for the potential treatment of Alzheimer's disease; and AL050, a GCase enzyme replacement therapy in preclinical development for the potential treatment of Parkinson's disease and Lewy body dementia in patients having GBA1 gene mutations. The company also develops its preclinical and research pipeline comprising AL064, a tau siRNA for Alzheimer's disease and other tauopathies; ADP062-ABC, an alpha-synuclein siRNA for Parkinson's disease; and ADP065-ABC, an NLRP3 siRNA for neurodegenerative conditions. It has a strategic collaboration agreement with GlaxoSmithKline plc for the development and commercialization of progranulin-elevating monoclonal antibodies, including Latozinemab and Nivisnebart. The company was founded in 2013 and is headquartered in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Arnon  Rosenthal Ph.D. | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 69 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 103 people. Revenue per employee of $204K ranks in the bottom quartile among Healthcare peers. Stock-based compensation of $259K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 5\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["Alector, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $378M market cap on $21M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -46% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","The company is burning through $184M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +14.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, thin -182.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 5.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 127% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 7.3% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Accruals elevated at +14.0% of assets \u2014 Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Piotroski score 1/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-4.7) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Healthcare peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 741% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Healthcare peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 62% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Alector (NASDAQ:ALEC) Stock Price Crosses Above Fifty Day Moving Average \u2013 Here\u2019s What Happened","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/alector-nasdaqalec-stock-price-crosses-above-fifty-day-moving-average-heres-what-happened.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793884885.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.791,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Alector Reports Third Quarter 2026 Financial Results and Provides Business Update","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/alector-reports-third-quarter-2026-210500378.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793912700.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.026,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"What Alector Doubters Missed","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-alec/alector/news/what-alector-doubters-missed","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793698483.885,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.612,"tier":1,"scope":"co